\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Successful-support coverage}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{support}

\p{For a task #{q}, policy #{\pi}, inference protocol #{D}, and budget #{b},
let #{\mathcal S^+(q)} be the trajectories accepted by the independent
evaluator. The \strong{successful-support probability} is}

##{
  p^+_{\pi,D,b}(q)
  =\Pr\{\tau\in\mathcal S^+(q)mid q,\pi,D,b\}.
}

\p{A training task law has \strong{successful-support coverage} at threshold
#{\varepsilon>0} for a task family if it assigns positive mass to tasks on
which #{p^+_{\pi,D,b}(q)\geq\varepsilon}. This is an FTIP specialization of
probabilistic support and coverage.}

\p{The threshold makes the definition finite and protocol-relative. It avoids
claiming that a successful sequence has exact zero probability after observing
only finitely many samples. The distinction between pass-at-one and broader
support is central to the experiments in \citef{yue2025does}.}
